      "text": "String-net condensation: A physical mechanism for topological phases — 18 sections: Front matter; Introduction; String-nets and gauge theories\n\n**String-net condensation: A physical mechanism for topological phases**\n\n*Michael A. Levin and Xiao-Gang Wen ∗*\n\n21 pp, 18 sections.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 String-nets and gauge theories; 3 General string-net picture; 4 String-net condensation in $(2+1)$ dimension; 4.1 Fixed-point wave functions; 4.2 Fixed-point Hamiltonians; 4.3 Quasiparticle excitations; 5 String-net condensation in $(3+1)$ and highe; 6 Examples; 6.1 $N=1$ string model; 6.2 $N=1$ string-net model; 6.3 $N = 2$ string-net models; 7 Conclusion; A General string-net models; B Self-consistency conditions; C Graphical representation of the Hamiltonian; D Graphical representation of the string opera",
